class.description:
A [Subtitle] holds [SubtitleSegment]s, each with a time range and a text. It knows nothing about audio or video: [SubtitleServer] plays it on a track, driven by any clock, for example the position of an [AudioStreamPlayer], a [VideoStreamPlayer] or an [AnimationPlayer], or its own clock.
The subtitle emits [signal Resource.changed] when one of its segments emits it, so an edit of a segment's times or text reaches everything that listens to the subtitle, such as [SubtitlePlayback].
Subtitle files load as [Subtitle] through [ResourceLoader], also from [code]user://[/code] and packs, and [ResourceSaver] writes them, in every format of [enum Format]: SubRip ([code].srt[/code]), WebVTT ([code].vtt[/code]), TTML/DFXP ([code].ttml[/code], [code].dfxp[/code]), SubStation Alpha ([code].ass[/code], [code].ssa[/code]) and YouTube SBV ([code].sbv[/code]). The extension picks the format. The rules below are those of SubRip; the other formats map their own speaker, italics and top placement (see [enum Format]). Styling is not read. Formatting is removed on loading: [code]<i>[/code], [code]<b>[/code], [code]<u>[/code], [code]<font>[/code] and [code]{\an8}[/code]-style tags. Kinds and speakers are recognized: a text fully in brackets ([code][Applause][/code] or [code](Applause)[/code]) becomes [constant SubtitleSegment.KIND_SOUND], a text between music notes becomes [constant SubtitleSegment.KIND_MUSIC], a leading name in capitals ([code]JOHN: Hello[/code]) becomes [member SubtitleSegment.speaker], and a text fully in [code]<i>[/code] sets [member SubtitleSegment.off_screen]. Saving writes these decorations back, so the file works in any video player. Saved as [code].tres[/code], every property is kept.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var subtitle: Subtitle = load("res://dialog/intro.srt")
subtitle.time_offset = -3600.0 # The file was exported from a timeline starting at 01:00:00.

SubtitleServer.text_changed.connect(func(_track_id, text): $SubtitleLabel.text = text)
SubtitleServer.play(subtitle, $Voice.get_playback_position)
$Voice.play()
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
var subtitle = GD.Load<Subtitle>("res://dialog/intro.srt");
subtitle.TimeOffset = -3600.0; // The file was exported from a timeline starting at 01:00:00.

SubtitleServer.Singleton.TextChanged += (trackId, text) => GetNode<Label>("SubtitleLabel").Text = text;
var voice = GetNode<AudioStreamPlayer>("Voice");
SubtitleServer.Play(subtitle, new Callable(voice, AudioStreamPlayer.MethodName.GetPlaybackPosition));
voice.Play();
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
